<title>UK: SBC Warburg rules out U.S. buy - paper.</title>
<headline>SBC Warburg rules out U.S. buy - paper.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>SBC Warburg, the investment banking arm of Swiss Bank Corp, has ruled out an immediate acquisition to boost its operations in the U.S., according to a report in the Financial Times.</p>
<p>The paper said SBC Warburg executive chairman Hans de Gier said he might opt to hire teams of traders who &quot;came loose&quot; from investment banks if U.S. commercial banks start a round of acquisitions on Wall Street.</p>
<p>De Gier said it was not in shareholders' interests to buy a U.S. operation at the moment since prices were unrealistically high, the paper said.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 4367</p>
